libsanitizer: find the mips stack pointer without glibc's EF_REG29

LeakSanitizer's stop-the-world reads each suspended thread's stack pointer out
of the ptrace register dump, and on mips it does so via EF_REG29, which glibc
declares in <sys/user.h>. musl ships <sys/user.h> and struct user but not that
constant, and the kernel's asm/reg.h that would supply it is not a uapi header,
so it is never installed into the sysroot. The build stops with

    sanitizer_stoptheworld_linux_libcdep.cpp:508: error: 'EF_REG29' was not
    declared in this scope

The index is fixed by the mips ptrace ABI rather than by any libc:
arch/mips/include/asm/reg.h places EF_R0 at 6 under CONFIG_32BIT, which puts
$sp (r29) at 35, and at 29 under CONFIG_64BIT. musl's struct user carries
regs[45+64], so both indices are in bounds. The SANITIZER_ANDROID branch
directly above already spells the same constant the kernel's way, EF_R29.

The ABI constants are defined locally rather than taken from
sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h. That header does supply them once patched,
and -Wundef confirms _ABI64 is visible here on gcc 13.3, but relying on it
couples two patches across three gcc versions -- and a constant that failed to
arrive would evaluate to 0 in the #if, silently choosing the 32-bit slot on a
64-bit target rather than failing to build.

Getting this wrong would not fail to build -- LSan would scan the wrong address
as a thread stack and quietly miss or invent leaks -- so the value is taken from
the kernel header in the tree rather than inferred.

Signed-off-by: OpenIPC AI team <ai@openipc.org>

--- a/libsanitizer/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_stoptheworld_linux_libcdep.cpp
+++ b/libsanitizer/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_stoptheworld_linux_libcdep.cpp
@@ -504,6 +504,28 @@
 typedef struct user regs_struct;
 # if SANITIZER_ANDROID
 #  define REG_SP regs[EF_R29]
+# elif !SANITIZER_GLIBC
+/* musl ships <sys/user.h> and struct user, but neither glibc's EF_REG29 nor
+   the kernel's asm/reg.h, which is not a uapi header and so is never
+   installed. The index is fixed by the mips ptrace ABI: arch/mips/include/
+   asm/reg.h puts EF_R0 at 6 under CONFIG_32BIT, making $sp (r29) 35, and 29
+   under CONFIG_64BIT. musl's struct user carries regs[45+64], so both are in
+   bounds. SANITIZER_ANDROID above already uses the kernel's spelling of the
+   same constant. */
+/* Defined locally rather than relied upon from sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h,
+   which does supply them once patched but is a coupling across three gcc
+   versions; an _ABI64 that failed to arrive would evaluate to 0 in the #if
+   below, silently selecting the 32-bit slot on a 64-bit target. */
+#  if !defined(_ABI64)
+#   define _ABIO32 1
+#   define _ABIN32 2
+#   define _ABI64  3
+#  endif
+#  if defined(_MIPS_SIM) && (_MIPS_SIM == _ABI64)
+#   define REG_SP regs[29]
+#  else
+#   define REG_SP regs[35]
+#  endif
 # else
 #  define REG_SP regs[EF_REG29]
 # endif
